<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<module fritzingVersion="1.0.2" moduleId="makerbuddy-iot-kit-v1-0-green-r2" referenceFile="makerbuddy-iot-kit-v1-green.fzp">
 <version>1</version>
 <author>MakerBuddy (https://makerbuddy.cc)</author>
 <title>MakerBuddy IoT Kit V1.0 (green)</title>
 <label>MB</label>
 <date>2026-11-24</date>
 <url>https://github.com/MakerBuddy/MakerBuddy-IoT-Kit-Fritzing-Parts</url>
 <tags>
  <tag>MakerBuddy</tag>
  <tag>IoT Kit</tag>
  <tag>ESP32</tag>
  <tag>ESP32 DevKit</tag>
  <tag>learning board</tag>
  <tag>JST-XH</tag>
  <tag>microcontroller</tag>
 </tags>
 <properties>
  <property name="family">MakerBuddy IoT Kit board</property>
  <property name="type">ESP32 carrier board</property>
  <property name="soldermask">green</property>
  <property name="revision">PCB V1.0</property>
  <property name="size">76 x 72.3 mm</property>
  <property name="processor">ESP32 (30-pin DevKit)</property>
  <property name="supply">5 V over USB</property>
 </properties>
 <description>MakerBuddy IoT Kit V1.0 learning board, green soldermask (the purple board is the same design). A 30-pin ESP32 DevKit sits in the middle of a 76 × 72.3 mm carrier with seven 3-pin connectors (26, 25, 33, 32, 23, 19, 18: signal, VCC, GND), an HC-SR04 connector (VCC, GND, 2, 15), a UART connector (VCC, GND, TX 17, RX 16), three I2C positions (VCC, GND, SCL 22, SDA 21), a 5V connector, VCC and GND rows, and a row of breakout holes beside each DevKit pin row. VCC is the DevKit's VIN pin: 5 V from USB. On the board itself: push button (GPIO 5), LED (12), RGB LED (13, 14, 27), potentiometer (34), light sensor (35), buzzer (4) and a 4.7 k pull-up on connector 26. https://makerbuddy.cc</description>
